<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Modules\{{ModuleName}}\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\JsonResponse;
use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Mk\Director\Auth\Controllers\BaseAuthController;
use Mk\Director\Auth\Models\AuthUser;

/**
 * {{ModuleName}}Controller (thin wrapper) — auth del scope `{{moduleNameLower}}`.
 *
 * ============================================================
 *  R-PKG-047 D1 + D2 — Patron BaseAuthController canónico
 * ============================================================
 *
 * Pre-R-PKG-047, este controller era una copia de ~500 LOC del AuthController
 * scaffoldeado (login/refresh/logout/me/forgot/reset/verifyEmail/etc. duplicados
 * 90% entre scopes). Bugs se fijaban per-scope y el scaffolder pineaba
 * placeholders condicionales `{{rbacAudit*}}`, `{{verifyEmailMethods}}` que
 * generaban N variantes.
 *
 * Post-R-PKG-047 D1, TODA la lógica vive en
 * `Mk\Director\Auth\Controllers\BaseAuthController` (SSoT canónico). Este thin
 * wrapper solo override los 4 abstracts requeridos:
 *
 *   - `authModelClass()` → FQCN del modelo del scope (pine la login field, tabla, etc.)
 *   - `authScope()` → 'admin', 'member', etc. (gate de middleware + ability)
 *   - `loginField()` → 'email', 'ci', 'phone', etc. (validation + lookup key)
 *   - `passwordResetTable()` → '{moduleNameLower}_password_reset_tokens' (D2 default)
 *
 * Total: ~30 LOC (vs ~500 LOC pre-D2). Para custom behaviour, override los
 * hooks provistos por BaseAuthController:
 *
 *   - `beforeLogin(Request, array)` — mod credentials pre-lookup (e.g. E.164 normalize)
 *   - `afterLogin(Request, Authenticatable, array)` — audit / analytics post-token-issue
 *   - `customizeLoginValidationRules()` — añade rules extra al /login (e.g. CI regex)
 *   - `customizeMePayload(Authenticatable)` — merge fields al /me response
 *   - `shouldSendResetNotification(Authenticatable, string)` — gate pre-email send
 *
 * ============================================================
 *  Endpoints expuestos (heredados de BaseAuthController, pineados via routes stub)
 * ============================================================
 *
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/login              — {{loginField}} + password → tokens
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/refresh            — refresh_token → access_token
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/logout             — revoca access token actual
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/logout-all         — revoca TODOS los tokens
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/password/forgot    — genera token reset
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/password/reset     — aplica reset con token
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/password/change    — cambia con current check
 *   GET    /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/me                 — usuario actual + abilities
 *   GET    /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/email/verify/{id}/{hash} — verify email (si --login-field=email)
 *   POST   /api/{{moduleNameLower}}/auth/email/resend       — reenviar verification (si --login-field=email)
 *
 * Auth + ability pineados PER-ROUTE en `auth-user.routes.stub` (no en constructor
 * per HALLAZGO-NEW-FASE18-C defense-in-depth): cada ruta lleva
 * `mk.auth:{{moduleNameLower}}` + `mk.ability:{{moduleNameLower}}.auth.{action}`.
 *
 * ============================================================
 *  Compat / BC notes
 * ============================================================
 *
 * - **Pre-R-PKG-047 AuthController scaffoldeado (~500 LOC)** sigue funcionando
 *   sin cambios — `extends BaseController` y los métodos heredan via
 *   copy-paste. La diferencia es solo estética: el scaffolder ahora emite
 *   thin wrapper (`extends BaseAuthController`) en vez de código duplicado.
 *   Consumers pre-existentes NO se rompen si regeneran post-R-PKG-047 —
 *   el thin wrapper es BEHAVIORAL EQUIVALENT al código anterior.
 *
 * - **Hooks nuevos (R-PKG-047)**: pre-R-PKG-047 no existen. Consumers que
 *   necesiten lógica custom (e.g. E.164 normalization) override los hooks
 *   en ESTE thin wrapper. Override opcional y BC-safe.
 *
 * - **ScopeStatus enum post-D4** (R-PKG-047 D4): el modelo del scope puede
 *   añadir `use ScopeStatus;` + cast `protected $casts = ['status' => ScopeStatus::class]`
 *   para reemplazar `is_active` boolean. `userHasValidStatus()` en
 *   BaseAuthController chequea el enum via `canAuthenticate()` con BC fallback
 *   a `is_active` boolean para scopes pre-D4.
 *
 * - **--verify-email**: si --login-field=email (default), la verificación está
 *   activa. Si --login-field=ci/phone/documento, los endpoints
 *   `/email/verify/...` retornan 422 ERR_VALIDATION (defense-in-depth contra
 *   pinear verificación sobre un campo que no es email).
 *
 * - **Enforcement de login-field (R-PKG-047 D5)**: BaseAuthController usa
 *   `$this->loginField()` dinámicamente en TODOS los endpoints de auth (no solo
 *   `login()`). Validation rules, lookup columns, Resource exposure, etc.
 *   Cambiar `--login-field=ci` regenera correctamente todos los 9 artifacts
 *   (F5 D5).
 *
 * Generado por `php artisan mk:make:auth-user {{ModuleName}}` post-R-PKG-047 D2.
 * Sin flags `--with-*` requiere (defaults ON: CRUD + RBAC + Status auto-pineados).
 */
class AuthController extends BaseAuthController
{
    /**
     * R-PKG-047 D1 — FQCN del modelo del scope.
     *
     * El scaffolder resuelve esto desde el argumento `{scope}` y pinea el FQCN
     * en runtime. Post-construcción, el modelo está en
     * `App\Modules\{{ModuleName}}\Models\{{ModuleName}}.php` extends `AuthUser`.
     *
     * @return class-string<\App\Modules\{{ModuleName}}\Models\{{ModuleName}}>
     */
    protected function authModelClass(): string
    {
        return \App\Modules\{{ModuleName}}\Models\{{ModuleName}}::class;
    }

    /**
     * R-PKG-047 D1 — scope string para middleware + tokens + abilities.
     *
     * Convention: snake_case del scope name. Pineado por el scaffolder desde
     * `{scope}` argument vía `Str::snake()`. Ej: Member → 'member', CustomerAdmin → 'customer_admin'.
     */
    protected function authScope(): string
    {
        return '{{moduleNameLower}}';
    }

    /**
     * R-PKG-047 D1 — campo usado para login (validation + lookup).
     *
     * Pineado desde `--login-field=` flag (default 'email'). Valores comunes:
     * 'email', 'ci', 'phone', 'username', 'documento'. BaseAuthController usa
     * dinámicamente en TODOS los endpoints (no hardcoded).
     */
    protected function loginField(): string
    {
        return '{{loginField}}';
    }

    /**
     * R-PKG-047 D1 — tabla donde se persisten los tokens de password reset.
     *
     * Convention: `{moduleNameLower}_password_reset_tokens`. La migration scaffoldeada
     * crea esta tabla con columnas `{loginField}` (UNIQUE), `token` (bcrypt-hash),
     * `created_at`. BaseAuthController la referencia via `DB::table($this->passwordResetTable())`
     * y `Schema::hasTable($table)` runtime check.
     */
    protected function passwordResetTable(): string
    {
        return '{{moduleNameLower}}_password_reset_tokens';
    }
}
